From e577d4b05543f99dfbc6ba5cd29ac1f15435b0b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:09:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel material properties: statistics and output
 status as for the behaviours

The evaluation of a material property reports the number of points where
it failed, the first of them, and the number of points where a bound is
violated with the warning policy, as the integration of the behaviours.
The kernels compute the status of each point, merged in the statistics
only when an event occurs: with integer atomic operations (CUDA, HIP,
SYCL, Kokkos), or by a reduction (parallel algorithms, OpenMP), as for the
behaviours. The cost is null when the evaluation succeeds.

The output status (mfront_gpmp_OutputStatus) and the statistics
(mfront_gpmp_Statistics, initialized by mfront_gpmp_initializeStatistics)
are specific to the interface. The execution options have the members of
the options of the behaviours: queue, statistics (asynchronous evaluation),
preservation of the stack size. The array of statuses and the
<name>_generic_parallel_number_of_statuses symbol are removed. The
<name>_generic_parallel_report function analyses the statistics.

The evaluation at a point is written in a lambda capturing by copy:
nvc++ 25.11 (-mp=gpu) does not write through a pointer captured by
reference by such a lambda in an OpenMP target region.
